-- title:
--   For a high-surplus probe, choose the pivot distribution before checking any successor.
-- statement:
--   For a high-surplus probe, choose the pivot distribution before checking any successor.
--   Every pivot of positive probability is admissible. Success at any such pivot makes the
--   common upper band correctly labelled and forces the expected gain to be at least 1/2.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.PriceGame.Charging.exists_probe_test`.
